and in business.<br/>  You use the passive voice when focusing on the person or thing affected by an action. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Here is an active sentence:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> Another swimmer saw the boy and the dolphin.</span><br/>(Subject + verb + object)<br/> The other swimmer is the focus of the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here is a passive sentence:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The boy and the dolphin <span class=\"strong\">were seen </span> (by another swimmer).</span><br/>(Passive subject + To Be + Past Participle) <br/>The boy and the dolphin are the focus of the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Caleb was swept out into the ocean and was unable to swim back. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A child feared drowned was discovered safe and sound. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Second Conditional - Talking About Hypothetical Situations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "  You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No. <br/>Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really. <br/>What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past verb + <span class=\"italic\">would</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"IF\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I married Peter,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would be happy.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">it snowed next July,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would be very surprised</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I were you,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would be jumping up and down.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If Angel could understand English, I would tell him that I love him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I would be a dolphin if I could be an animal.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to fear ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be afraid of ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A child was feared drowned.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about nature.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "safe and sound ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "free from danger or injury ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The child was discovered safe and sound.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "miraculously", "type": "name"}, {"content": " in a way that goes against laws of the universe  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Miraculously, a dolphin carried the boy to safety.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to spot ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to see", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: The dolphin spotted the boy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to slip", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to enter a place quietly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Caleb slipped into the water.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "miracle", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a surprising event considered to be the result of divine intervention ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's a real miracle!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go online and find a short English news article.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Underline all the past passive verbs you see.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down all the verbs you find.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make